  "_meta": {
    "notes": "The picture the corner mark exists for. All four kerbals stand Available on KSP's own roster, which is what the Astronaut Complex files them under and all it has to go on; two of them are on RP-1 courses and one of those has not been started. Retirement is off for this save and nobody has training lapsing, so the block under each name is at most the one line naming the course, and the four cards are otherwise identical. Scanning them for a crew who could fly, the corner is what answers and the block is what is skipped.",
    "why-not-the-schedule-block": "The mark used to lead the 'Course' line in the block under the name. That block is read once an operator has settled on a kerbal; whether a kerbal is on a course at all is what decides which one they settle on, and on a card with no other RP-1 dates the block does not render at all. crew-schedule-three-states is the picture of the block; this is the picture of the corner."
  },
